Automated tests
===============

    ./test/run_all.sh

runs everything below (needs PlatformIO, Node 18+, Python 3):

  test/check_wiring.py             config.h <-> README wiring table + ESP32 pin safety
  tools/wiring_diagram.py --check  the diagrams in docs/wiring/ match config.h
  test/backend/appsscript.test.js  backend/AppsScript.gs against a fake spreadsheet
  test/test_native/test_main.cpp   firmware logic on the host (pio test -e native);
                                   Arduino String / Preferences come from test/mocks/
  pio run -e hardware              the ESP32 firmware compiles warning-free

The mocks are deliberately strict: the Preferences mock rejects NVS keys
longer than 15 characters like real flash does, and "rebooting" in a test
means building fresh objects over the same mock flash.

Hardware acceptance checks (manual, on the real board)
------------------------------------------------------

Do README.md's "Bring it up in stages" first. Then, with the serial monitor
open (`pio device monitor`, 115200) and two enrolled cards A and B plus one
un-enrolled card X:

1.  Boot: log shows "OLED found at I2C 0x3C", "MFRC522 version 0x.. (OK)",
    "Wi-Fi connected", "Clock set via NTP" and no [CONFIG] lines; OLED shows
    SYSTEM READY / Wi-Fi: Connected.
2.  Tap A: green LED + beep + "WELCOME!" at once, then "ATTENDANCE LOGGED"
    when the upload is confirmed; a row appears in the Sheet.
3.  Tap A again after ~3 s: red LED, "ALREADY LOGGED", no new row.
4.  Tap X: red LED, "ACCESS DENIED", its UID in the log.
5.  Non-blocking: `RESET`, then tap A and B within a second of each other.
    B's "WELCOME!" appears immediately, without waiting for A's upload.
6.  `ENROLL Test Student`, then tap X -> "STUDENT ADDED". `LIST` shows it.
    Unplug/replug: still enrolled. `REMOVE <X's UID>` -> gone, also after
    a replug.
7.  `ADD 3F2A9B11 Other Student` works; `ADD 3F 2A 9B 11 X` is rejected
    ("8 or 14 hex digits"); a duplicate UID is rejected.
8.  Short-press the reset button: "Present: X / Y", returns to ready on its
    own, nobody's status changes.
9.  Unplug/replug: a card that was logged still says ALREADY LOGGED (once
    the clock is set, a few seconds after boot).
10. Hold the reset button while plugging in, release when the screen says
    so: attendance wiped, enrolled students kept. Releasing before 3 s
    cancels.
11. Offline/outbox: turn the hotspot off, tap an enrolled card ->
    "Saved (offline)" and "Unsynced: 1" on the ready screen. Turn it back
    on: the tap uploads by itself within about a minute, with the time it
    was TAPPED, and "Unsynced" disappears.
12. Wrong API key in secrets.h (reflash): tap -> "SAVED LOCALLY ... Check
    API key!", "Unsynced" stays and retries with growing delay ([SYNC] log).
    Put the right key back and reflash: the queued tap uploads.
13. `STATUS` prints Wi-Fi, clock, day, queue, reader, OLED and heap.
    `SELFTEST` blinks all three LEDs and beeps twice.
14. Next day (or after midnight): the first tap of the day is accepted -
    yesterday's "present" flags are cleared as soon as the clock is set.
